-- title:
--   Domain criterion for k⊗_𝔽κ from a degree count
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathbb F$, $k$, $\kappa$, $\Omega$ be fields in one universe, with $k$ and $\kappa$ algebras over $\mathbb F$, and let $\kappa$ carry in addition an algebra structure over the polynomial ring $\mathbb F[X]$ compatible with its $\mathbb F$-algebra structure; write $x := \mathrm{algebraMap}\,\mathbb F[X]\,\kappa\,X$ for the image of $X$ in $\kappa$ and $\mathbb F(x) :=$ `IntermediateField.adjoin 𝔽 {x}` for the $\mathbb F$-subfield of $\kappa$ it generates. Assume $\kappa$ is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb F(x)$. Let $\Omega$ be an algebra over $k$ and over $\mathbb F$, compatibly, and let $\rho\colon\kappa\to\Omega$ be an $\mathbb F$-algebra homomorphism such that $\rho(x)$ is transcendental over $k$. Inside the $k$-subfield $E :=$ `IntermediateField.adjoin k (Set.range ρ)` of $\Omega$ generated by the image of $\rho$, consider the $k$-subfield generated by $\rho(x)$, and assume the degree inequality $[\kappa:\mathbb F(x)] \le [E : k(\rho(x))]$ between the corresponding `Module.finrank`s. The conclusion is that the commutative ring $k\otimes_{\mathbb F}\kappa$ is a domain, i.e. nontrivial and without zero divisors. (Transcendence of $\rho(x)$ over $k$ forces $x$ transcendental over $\mathbb F$, so $\mathbb F(x)$ is a rational function field; this is a consequence of the hypotheses rather than an assumption.)
--
--   This is a linear-disjointness criterion of the classical Deuring–Igusa type: the degree count says that the multiplication map $k\otimes_{\mathbb F}\kappa\to\Omega$, $a\otimes y\mapsto a\,\rho(y)$, cannot collapse, so $k$ and $\kappa$ are linearly disjoint over $\mathbb F$ and the tensor product is a domain. It is used in the construction of two-chart integral models of curves, where it shows that a chart algebra remains a domain after base change along $\mathbb F\to k$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_IntermediateField_isDomain_tensorProduct_of_finrank_le_finrank_adjoin_range.lean

